## ✍ DM Response
As twilight cloaks Camelot in its shroud, you, Sioned ferch Cai, tread the familiar path from Avalon's yew tree portal to the hallowed court of King Arthur. The once vibrant city now seems diminished, the air heavy with a palpable tension that was not there before. You hold close your ancient ledger, its pages marked by an entry you can now decipher two more words of - but at what cost?

Upon reaching Camelot's gates, you spot Peredur map Gwrtheyrn standing before an ancient shrine. His gaze is distant, lost in thought as he contemplates the mysteries that lie beyond the mortal realm. You approach him, calling out softly to break through his reverie.

"Peredur," you say with a trembling voice, "I have returned from Avalon. I have read more of the entry in my ledger, but it was not without consequence."

His eyes widen as he looks up at you, sensing the gravity in your words. He listens intently as you recount your experiences and share your newfound knowledge. You watch as the realization dawns upon him, his face clouding over with a mix of fear and determination.

"The Veil is growing weaker," he murmurs, "and Nimue will not be able to hold it back much longer." He pauses for a moment, then continues, "We must act quickly if we are to protect what remains of our world."

The wind picks up suddenly, carrying with it an eerie whisper that seems to echo from the depths of Avalon. The air grows colder, the shadows deeper, and you feel a sense of dread creeping in as though some malevolent force has taken notice of your conversation.

In the distance, the once-majestic Camelot stands watchful over the land, its towers shrouded in mist, its walls ominous and imposing. The city remains silent, its people unaware of the tumultuous events unfolding just beyond their doorsteps. As you stand there with Peredur, you cannot help but wonder what the future holds for you all - and whether the darkness that has returned from Avalon can truly be held at bay.

## 📋 Summary
Sioned ferch Cai returns to Camelot from Avalon with new information about the weakening Veil, causing concern for Peredur map Gwrtheyrn. Upon their encounter, Peredur acknowledges the severity of the situation and suggests they act quickly to protect their world, as an ominous wind hints at the presence of malevolent forces from Avalon. The majestic yet foreboding Camelot stands silent and unaware of the impending crisis.
